cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "caseload: reinforcement learning environments for budgeted fraud investigation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Suryavanshi
    given-names: Jayesh
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
abstract: >-
  Reinforcement learning environments for budgeted fraud investigation: deciding where
  to point scarce human review, and when, while the fraud population moves. The first
  environment is selective labels under a regime break, where investigating a case is
  the only way to reveal its label, so a policy that spends its whole budget on the
  highest-scoring cases stops learning when the fraud population shifts. It trains on
  procedurally generated drift and evaluates zero-shot on the real regime break in the
  Elliptic Bitcoin transaction graph. The second is capacity-constrained routing of
  synthetic bank-account-opening fraud alerts to 50 synthetic analysts on Feedzai's
  FiFAR dataset. Both share an evaluation harness with interquartile means,
  stratified bootstrap intervals, paired differences and oracle ceilings.
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/JayeshSuryavanshi/caseload"
keywords:
  - reinforcement-learning
  - fraud-detection
  - selective-labels
  - monitored-mdp
